From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 19:02:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07698/11362] [outer-loop] ARC oracle-perception goal ablation:
 does correct perception flip gemma's goal? (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5832)

Gates the perception-fix direction before building HUD/mover detectors: hand the
same gemma-4-31B the correct entities (what a perfect detector would output) and
measure whether its goal hypothesis flips to the true win condition. 3 conditions
(naive / +entities / +entities+HUD-labeled), 8 games, learned rules held constant,
no goal leaked into the perception facts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 scripts/arc_oracle_perception_goal_ablation.py | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/arc_oracle_perception_goal_ablation.py b/scripts/arc_oracle_perception_goal_ablation.py
index 501a613c9a..eaba12550d 100644
--- a/scripts/arc_oracle_perception_goal_ablation.py
+++ b/scripts/arc_oracle_perception_goal_ablation.py
@@ -137,9 +137,9 @@ def main() -> int:
     os.environ.setdefault("CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU", "1")  # outer-loop owns GPU 1
     from carnot.agentic.arc_executable_world_model import LocalGGUFProposer
 
-    # PRECONDITIONS: the 31B GGUF must be cached (fail honest, do not fabricate).
-    from carnot.agentic.arc_solver_kit import _hf_cache_has  # type: ignore[attr-defined]
-
+    # PRECONDITION is handled by LocalGGUFProposer._ensure_server(): if the GGUF is uncached or the
+    # llama-server fails to start, _complete() returns (False, reason) -- an honest failure datum, never
+    # a fabricated goal. So no separate cache check is needed.
     t0 = time.time()
     proposer = LocalGGUFProposer(
         repo_substr="gemma-4-31B-it",
